esult", "You must buy this", "This fixes the problem"], "evidence_note": "Evidence is required for any performance claim; otherwise replace it with personal-context wording.", "claim_boundary": "No medical claim, no financial claim, and no universal result promise. Frame this as creator context and decision support.", "disclosure_text": "If sponsored, use a clear #ad disclosure at the start of the caption and video.", "safer_alternative_phrase": "In my context, this is the cleaner decision."}, "caption_pack": {"cta": "Save this local atlas filter and use it before your next Luxury decision.", "on_screen_text": ["The hidden decision", "Keep / remove / why", "Save the filter"], "caption_options": ["The premium part is the local atlas you can explain.", "Save this before you copy the final shot from the phone notes screen.", "Less noise, clearer context, better Luxury decisions around popular but not always right."]}, "idea_summary": {"premise": "The creator reveals the hidden decision behind a polished Luxury content moment using a phone notes screen and a mistake correction.", "target_emotion": "The audience feels invited into a smarter, more premium way to choose when popular but not always right is handled clearly.", "creator_takeaway": "Show the decision process, not only the final result."}, "scene_script": [{"second": "0-3", "purpose": "attention", "voiceover": "The part that looks effortless is actually one small mistake correction.", "spoken_lines": ["Watch the decision before the result."], "on_screen_text": "The hidden decision"}, {"second": "4-10", "purpose": "premise", "voiceover": "For this Luxury moment, I start from the local atlas and the phone notes screen instead of adding more noise.", "spoken_lines": ["I start here."], "on_screen_text": "One filter first"}, {"second": "11-24", "purpose": "proof", "voiceover": "Here is the proof detail: mistake correction, what I kept, what I removed, and why it fits this context.", "spoken_lines": ["This is the boundary."], "on_screen_text": "Keep / remove / why"}, {"second": "25-34", "purpose": "payoff", "voiceover": "Save this if you want a cleaner way to make the same decision.", "spoken_lines": ["Save the filter, not just the final shot."], "on_screen_text": "Save the filter"}, {"second": "35-38", "purpose": "comment", "voiceover": "Tell me which option you would remove first.", "spoken_lines": ["What would you remove?"], "on_screen_text": "Comment your first remove"}], "variant_pack": {"reels": "38-second decision-filter Reel with hook, proof, payoff, and comment CTA.", "story": "Three-frame Story: poll, proof detail, checklist.", "carousel": "Five-slide decision filter with one proof example per slide.", "short_15s": "Final shot, hidden decision, one proof detail, save CTA.", "youtube_shorts": "Faster voiceover version with the same decision and proof structure."}, "editing_notes": {"sound": "Soft premium bed with light object sounds and clear voiceover.", "pacing": "Fast first cut, measured proof section, clean final checklist hold.", "transitions": ["hard cut from final to decision table", "caption pop for boundary", "held frame for save CTA"]}, "comment_engine": {"pinned_comment": "What would you remove from this decision first?", "reply_strategy": "Turn the strongest replies into a follow-up Story poll or a second decision-filter Reel.", "audience_question": "Which option would make this feel cleaner, safer, or more premium when popular but not always right is the problem?"}, "pose_direction": {"body": "Relaxed shoulders, slight angle to camera, stable posture.", "face": "Calm, focused, and slightly knowing.", "hands": "Use slow sorting gestures; avoid frantic pointing or constant product pushing.", "expression": "Confident but not exaggerated; let the proof carry the energy."}, "story_followup": {"poll_options": ["The hook", "The proof", "The edit", "The caption"], "poll_question": "Which part should I break down next?", "followup_frame": "Share the winning poll re